# NJ02 registry acceptance cases — independent semantic expectations
# Authority: NJ02RegistryIndependentCases.md, product 16060a72554d82849128a56c0960f847476f6b79
# Status: OLD facts frozen. New text surface/coordinates NOT FROZEN. New-arm cases NOT RUN.
# These are test requirements, not candidate DSL syntax or generated-output fixtures.

GROUP POSITIVE OLD FACTS

CASE R0a ordered constructions
  INPUT checked-in core constructions at pinned SHA
  EXPECT exactly seven IDs in ledger order, with exactly the listed axis and bilingual description values
  EXPECT core.agreement.possessive.axis and core.composite.axis are explicit Null
  EXPECT core.composite.composesOf is a present empty List
  EXPECT composesOf is Absent for each of the other six constructions
  STATUS old fact observed; candidate execution NOT RUN

CASE R0b ordered features
  INPUT checked-in core features at pinned SHA
  EXPECT exactly seven keys in ledger order and every values list in ledger order
  EXPECT each gloss retains its exact ru/en text, including Cyrillic punctuation
  EXPECT Person values are Text "1", "2", "3"
  STATUS old fact observed; candidate execution NOT RUN

CASE R0c accepted schema distinctions
  INPUT one independent registry variant per allowed state
  EXPECT axis: Absent, Text, and explicit Null are distinct accepted states
  EXPECT composesOf: Absent and present List([]) are distinct accepted states
  EXPECT description.en: Absent is accepted; description.ru: Absent is rejected
  EXPECT gloss: Absent, empty Record({}), and one-language Record are accepted
  EXPECT feature values: nonempty List<Text> with unique nonempty entries
  STATUS schema-derived expectations; candidate execution NOT RUN

GROUP EXISTING VALIDATOR PARITY
# OLD means supported by pinned schema/validator. It does not mean every mutation was run.
# No old token coordinate is claimed: the JSON validator reports schema/curriculum paths.

CASE R2b duplicate value within one feature values list
  MUTATE Case.values by adding a second "Nom" while retaining the first
  EXPECT reject via core-features schema uniqueItems; never silently deduplicate
  EXPECT new authoring diagnostic locates duplicate value and, where available, first occurrence
  OLD basis core-features schema uniqueItems; new-arm execution NOT RUN

CASE R5 unresolved curriculum construction
  MUTATE one curriculum construction from core.argument.case-role to core.does-not-exist
  EXPECT reject unknown construction against the seven-ID registry
  OLD basis checkConstructionsResolve; existing pack test mutates pl first skill
  EXPECT new source diagnostic locates the offending curriculum reference when that source is ported
  STATUS candidate execution NOT RUN

CASE R6a unresolved curriculum feature key
  MUTATE one focus.feature from Case to AbsentFeature; separately mutate a fixed key likewise
  EXPECT each rejected as a feature absent from the core registry
  OLD basis checkFeaturesResolve; candidate execution NOT RUN

CASE R6b unresolved curriculum feature value
  MUTATE one focus.from, one focus.to, and one fixed value to Impossible in separate inputs
  EXPECT each rejected as undeclared for its existing feature
  OLD basis checkFeaturesResolve; candidate execution NOT RUN

CASE R7 feature not enabled by language
  MUTATE a language usesFeatures to omit a feature used by its curriculum while retaining that core feature
  EXPECT reject used feature absent from lang/<code>/lang.json usesFeatures
  OLD basis checkFeaturesResolve; candidate execution NOT RUN

CASE R8a malformed nested description
  MUTATE one construction description to omit ru; separately set ru to empty text, a number, or a list
  EXPECT each rejected by core-constructions schema at the nested description
  EXPECT omitted en accepted; present empty en rejected
  OLD basis required/type/minLength; candidate execution NOT RUN

CASE R8b malformed nested gloss and feature values
  MUTATE one gloss.ru or gloss.en to empty text or a number in separate inputs
  MUTATE one values item to empty text or a number; separately make values empty
  EXPECT each rejected by core-features schema at the nested gloss/value or list
  EXPECT omitted gloss, empty gloss record, and omitted one language member accepted
  OLD basis type/minLength/minItems; candidate execution NOT RUN

CASE R8c construction optional types
  MUTATE one axis to a number; separately mutate one composesOf item to a number
  EXPECT each rejected by core-constructions schema
  EXPECT axis Null and composesOf List([]) remain accepted
  OLD basis type constraints; candidate execution NOT RUN

GROUP NEW AUTHORING PROFILE AND PIPELINE
# NEW cases apply equally to A/B/C. They are not old JSON validator parity.

CASE R1 duplicate construction source key
  MUTATE new authored source to declare core.number twice
  EXPECT reject duplicate ID; diagnostic identifies second declaration and both origins
  REASON JSON.parse collapses duplicate object keys before old schema/checks
  STATUS proposed independently; source coordinates NOT FROZEN; NOT RUN

CASE R2a duplicate feature source key
  MUTATE new authored source to declare Case twice
  EXPECT reject duplicate key; diagnostic identifies second declaration and both origins
  REASON JSON.parse collapses duplicate object keys before old schema/checks
  STATUS proposed independently; source coordinates NOT FROZEN; NOT RUN

CASE R9a stale source
  AFTER clean candidate generation mutate one authored registry fact only
  EXPECT candidate freshness check fails for dependent outputs before accepted build
  STATUS proposed independently; artifact identity/command NOT FROZEN; NOT RUN

CASE R9b stale binding
  AFTER clean candidate generation mutate a fact binding/read plan only
  EXPECT candidate contract/freshness check fails, with no stale accepted output
  STATUS proposed independently; artifact identity/command NOT FROZEN; NOT RUN

CASE R9c stale output
  AFTER clean candidate generation mutate generated typed output only
  EXPECT that output's own freshness check fails
  STATUS proposed independently; artifact identity/command NOT FROZEN; NOT RUN

EXCLUDED FROM ACCEPTED OLD PARITY
  R3 unknown axis: schema permits arbitrary Text; validator does not resolve axis.
  R4 absent/wrong-kind composesOf target or cycle: schema permits Text items; validator does not resolve or traverse them.
  These need a separately accepted owner requirement and independent oracle before becoming comparison cases.

SOURCE COORDINATE FREEZE RULE
  For each arm, first pin the concrete new source file and hash. Then author each mutation above,
  record exact file/line/column of the offending token and both origins for duplicate keys,
  and commit that expectation before running the new implementation. Until then: NOT FROZEN.
  Never read the compiler's observed location to fill an expected coordinate.
